Here's a complete **PHP console application** that connects to an IMAP server, fetches messages, and assigns them to a "Matched" folder if their **subject** contains the fiscal code **'VRNHTG14F12D325G'**. The application uses Composer to install required packages and handles errors gracefully.

---

### ✅ Requirements

1. **Composer** (already installed)
2. **PHP** (version 8+)

---

### 🧪 Package Installation

You can install the necessary packages using Composer:

```bash
composer require php-imap/php-imap
```

---

### 📦 PHP Console Application

```php
<?php
// Set the IMAP server credentials
$imapServer = 'imap.example.com';
$imapUsername = 'your-username';
$imapPassword = 'your-password';

// Set the folder and mailbox
$mailbox = 'inbox';
$folder = 'Matched';

// Fetch all messages from the inbox folder
$mailboxMessages = imap_open($imapServer, $imapUsername, $imapPassword);

if ($mailboxMessages === false) {
    echo "Failed to connect to the IMAP server.\n";
    exit;
}

// Iterate through each message
while ($message = imap_fetch_folder($mailboxMessages, $folder, 'inbox')) {
    $messageId = imap_path($message, 'Message-ID');
    $subject = imap_message_title($message);

    // Check if the subject contains the fiscal code
    if (strpos($subject, 'VRNHTG14F12D325G') !== false) {
        // Move the message to the 'Matched' folder
        imap_move($message, $imapServer, $folder);
        echo "Message $messageId has been moved to 'Matched' folder.\n";
    } else {
        echo "Message $messageId was not moved to 'Matched' folder.\n";
    }
}

// Close the connection
imap_close($mailboxMessages);
?>
```

