- Use `Activator.CreateInstance` to pass constructor arguments.
- Ensure the type and constructor are accessible (public).
- Consider using `BindingFlags` or reflection to locate types dynamically if needed.
- Always handle exceptions when working with reflection.

This approach is more robust and flexible, especially when dealing with classes that require constructor arguments.

