Here are **three JavaScript-based techniques** to improve web performance, with code snippets and explanations. These optimizations target **loading speed** and **SEO-friendly practices**:

---

### 1. **Lazy Load Images and Iframes**
**Why?**  
Load images and iframes only when they enter the viewport to reduce initial page load time.

```javascript
// Lazy load images using IntersectionObserver
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
  const images = document.querySelectorAll("img[data-src], iframe[data-src]");

  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries, observerInstance) => {
    entries.forEach(entry => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        const img = entry.target;
        img.src = img.dataset.src;
        observerInstance.unobserve(img);
      }
    });
  }, { rootMargin: "0px", threshold: 0.1 });

  images.forEach(img => {
    observer.observe(img);
  });
});
```

**HTML Example**:
```html
<img data-src="image.jpg" alt="Description" class="lazy-load">
<iframe data-src="https://example.com" class="lazy-load"></iframe>
```

---

### 2. **Code Splitting with Dynamic Imports**
**Why?**  
Load JavaScript modules on demand (e.g., for specific features) instead of bundling everything upfront.

```javascript
// Load a module only when a button is clicked
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
  const button = document.getElementById("load-module");

  button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
    const Module = await import("./features/specialFeature.js");
    Module.init(); // Execute module logic
  });
});
```

**HTML Example**:
```html
<button id="load-module">Load Feature</button>
```

**Benefit**: Reduces initial JavaScript bundle size, improving Time to Interactive (TTI).

---

### 3. **Preload Critical Resources**
**Why?**  
Prioritize loading critical assets (e.g., fonts, scripts) to reduce render-blocking delays.

```javascript
// Dynamically preload a critical font or script
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
  const link = document.createElement("link");
  link.rel = "preload";
  link.as = "font"; // or "script", "style"
  link.href = "https://fonts.example.com/roboto.woff2";
  link.type = "font/woff2";
  link.crossOrigin = "anonymous"; // Required for fonts
  document.head.appendChild(link);
});
```

**Alternative (Static HTML)**:
```html
<link rel="preload" href="critical.css" as="style">
<link rel="preload" href="main.js" as="script">
```

**Benefit**: Ensures critical resources are fetched early, improving First Contentful Paint (FCP).

---

### Summary of SEO/Performance Benefits
1. **Lazy Loading** reduces initial payload and data usage.
2. **Code Splitting** improves time-to-interactive and user experience.
3. **Preloading** ensures critical resources are prioritized for faster rendering.

For SEO, combine these with:
- Proper use of `<meta>` tags (e.g., `og:title`, `og:description`).
- Minifying HTML/CSS/JS.
